  "id": "Compound::DB00141 - Gene::8704",
  "verbalization": "N-acetyl-d-glucosamine is implicated in the regulation of B4galt2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that N-acetyl-d-glucosamine binds to B4galt4 and B4galt3, which in turn participate in N-acetyllactosamine Synthase Activity. This activity is then recognized by B4galt2, indicating a hierarchical relationship where N-acetyl-d-glucosamine influences B4galt2 via intermediate proteins. The shared involvement of B4galt2 in Lactose Synthase Activity in Path 3 further suggests a broader role in glycosylation processes. The consistent scores across the paths indicate a robust, though indirect, connection between N-acetyl-d-glucosamine and B4galt2, likely mediated through the N-acetyllactosamine Synthase Activity. The mechanism appears to involve a regulatory pathway where N-acetyl-d-glucosamine modulates the activity of B4galt2 through its interaction with other glycosyltransferase enzymes.",
